# CMake build directories. Underscore, hyphen, and bare-numeric-suffix
# variants are all ignored (Ilia/Amelia review finding on tasks
# 0012/0013: ad-hoc build dirs like `build-shuosher/`/`build-ilia/` used
# only an underscore pattern previously and showed up as untracked
# cruft; task 0015 review found the same gap for numeric-suffix dirs
# like `build2/`/`build3/`, used by independent reviewer rebuilds run
# from this same worktree).
build/
build[0-9]*/
build_*/
build-*/
cmake-build-*/

# Editor/OS cruft
.DS_Store
*.swp

# Ad-hoc local benchmark reruns. Accepted reference baselines are committed
# explicitly (see BENCHMARKS.md #10) rather than ignored wholesale.
benchmarks/results/*.local.csv

# Generated VTK visualization output (tutorials/scalar_advection_3d_visualization/) --
# regenerated by running the tutorial, not committed.
vtk_output/

# Local Python virtual environments (tutorials/burgers_1d_shock_and_steepening/,
# tutorials/burgers_2d_diagonal_shock/ -- their READMEs suggest creating one
# to install numpy/pandas/matplotlib, but it must never be committed).
.venv/
__pycache__/

# Forward-step VTK snapshot data (tutorials/euler_2d_forward_step/,
# tutorials/euler_3d_forward_step_extrusion/) -- regenerated by running the
# tutorial; only figures/*.png and data/*/summary.csv are committed going
# forward, so this ignores the *.vtk frames specifically, not the whole
# data/ directory (summary.csv must stay trackable). Historical VTK frames
# already committed in prior commits are a separate cleanup question, not
# addressed by this ignore rule (git does not retroactively untrack
# already-committed files).
tutorials/euler_2d_forward_step/data/**/*.vtk
tutorials/euler_3d_forward_step_extrusion/data/**/*.vtk
